{"understanding":"HashiCorp Raft is a Go replicated-log library with follower, candidate, and leader execution loops. Leaders persist log entries locally, replicate them through an injected Transport, advance commitment, and apply committed entries through an FSM. Followers validate AppendEntries prefixes, truncate conflicting suffixes, persist received entries, update commit/application state, and can install snapshots. Configuration entries are represented in the log and tracked separately as committed/latest configurations. StableStore, LogStore, SnapshotStore, Transport, and FSM are injected interfaces; concrete backend behavior and schedule control are not established by the supplied materials.","audit_spec":{"version":1,"target_profile":{"system_boundary":"The hashicorp/raft library from client API admission through Raft state transitions, log and stable-store access, transport RPC handling, replication, snapshot lifecycle, and FSM callbacks. Injected store, transport, and FSM implementations are boundary dependencies.","protocol_contexts":["follower","candidate","leader","pre-vote and vote handling","AppendEntries replication","InstallSnapshot recovery","protocol versions 0 through current supported versions","configuration changes and leadership transfer"],"external_interfaces":["Transport RPCs and AppendEntries pipelines","LogStore","StableStore","SnapshotStore","FSM and optional BatchingFSM","client futures and notification channels","observer callbacks"],"ownership":["main Raft thread owns state transitions, RPC processing, configuration state, commit progression, and client request dispatch","replication goroutines own per-peer AppendEntries and snapshot transmission","FSM thread owns application and FSM snapshot capture","injected stores own persistence and deletion semantics","Transport implementation owns message delivery, response behavior, and optional heartbeat fast path"],"selection_injection":["Raft construction selects Config, Transport, LogStore, StableStore, SnapshotStore, and FSM implementations","protocol version and feature flags select compatibility and pre-vote/configuration paths","optional transport interfaces select pre-vote, close, and pipeline behavior","FSM type selects single-entry or batch application"],"variants":["protocol-version compatibility changes configuration log encoding","pre-vote enabled or disabled","single-entry FSM versus BatchingFSM","normal AppendEntries replication versus pipeline replication","log replay versus InstallSnapshot when a follower is behind retained logs","automatic versus user-triggered snapshots","voter, non-voter, staging, and removed participant states","leadership transfer path"],"source_ids":["README.md:1:80","docs/README.md:1:80","transport.go:1:80","config.go:1:80","fsm.go:1:80"],"unknowns":["The supplied material does not establish the concrete store implementations or their atomicity and durability guarantees.","The supplied material does not include the complete client API, future resolution, FSM loop, snapshot installation completion, or startup restoration paths.","No deterministic schedule or crash/restart execution control is available.","The active protocol-version range and exact configuration behavior for every supported version are not fully visible in the supplied excerpts."]},"activities":[{"class_id":"A1","applicability":"applicable","purpose":"Form, persist, replicate, and advance replicated log decisions and commitment.","realization_summary":"Leader dispatchLogs assigns index and term, stores entries locally, records local replication, and notifies per-peer replication routines. Replication updates per-peer progress and commitment after successful AppendEntries or snapshot transfer. Followers accept validated entries and advance commit processing from leader-provided commit indices.","entry_points":["Raft.runLeader","Raft.dispatchLogs","replication.replicate","replication.replicateTo","raft.appendEntries"],"variants":["ordinary AppendEntries","AppendEntries pipeline","replication fallback after pipeline errors","snapshot transfer when LogStore lookup returns ErrLogNotFound"],"unknowns":["The supplied excerpts do not show commitment quorum calculation, commit notification, or all stale-response handling.","The supplied excerpts do not establish how persistence failures interact with already issued replication responses."],"source_ids":["raft.go:468:700","raft.go:1203:1390","replication.go:137:388","raft.go:1440:1605","log.go:1:80"]},{"class_id":"A2","applicability":"applicable","purpose":"Acquire, change, lose, and interpret Raft authority and term context.","realization_summary":"The main loop selects follower, candidate, or leader behavior. Follower heartbeat expiry can enter candidate state; candidates perform pre-vote or vote collection; incoming AppendEntries or vote requests with newer terms update term and may force follower state. Leaders step down on relevant signals and resolve in-flight operations with leadership-loss errors.","entry_points":["Raft.run","Raft.runFollower","Raft.runCandidate","Raft.runLeader","raft.appendEntries","raft.requestVote","raft.requestPreVote"],"variants":["pre-vote enabled","pre-vote disabled","leadership transfer","newer-term AppendEntries","newer-term vote request","heartbeat timeout"],"unknowns":["The supplied excerpts do not show the complete election tally and leader-transition persistence path.","The exact legal relationship between persisted term/vote state and state transitions requires additional source review."],"source_ids":["raft.go:135:340","raft.go:468:700","raft.go:1440:1605","config.go:1:80"]},{"class_id":"A3","applicability":"applicable","purpose":"Restore lagging, restarted, disconnected, or snapshot-requiring participants to legal participation.","realization_summary":"A leader falls back to the latest stored snapshot when a follower is too far behind retained logs. It sends snapshot metadata and data through InstallSnapshot and, on success, advances the follower replication index and commitment tracking. The receiver-side installation and restart reconstruction are not included in the supplied excerpts.","entry_points":["replication.sendLatestSnapshot","Transport.InstallSnapshot","raft.installSnapshot"],"variants":["incremental log replay","snapshot installation after log retention gap","snapshot rejection or transport failure","newer-term snapshot response"],"unknowns":["Receiver-side snapshot validation, FSM restore, log replacement, and post-restore index reconstruction are not shown.","Startup recovery from LogStore, StableStore, and SnapshotStore is not shown.","Snapshot transfer completion does not by itself establish FSM restoration in the supplied evidence."],"source_ids":["replication.go:137:388","snapshot.go:72:278","transport.go:1:80","fsm.go:1:80"]},{"class_id":"A4","applicability":"applicable","purpose":"Create, encode, persist, commit, activate, and consume participant configuration versions.","realization_summary":"Configuration changes derive a new configuration from the latest configuration, validate unique IDs and addresses and at least one voter, encode a compatibility-specific log entry, dispatch it, update latest configuration state, and restart peer replication. Received configuration entries update committed/latest configuration tracking. At most one uncommitted configuration is represented by the tracked state.","entry_points":["nextConfiguration","Raft.appendConfigurationEntry","Raft.processConfigurationLogEntry","configurationChangeChIfStable","checkConfiguration"],"variants":["protocol version below 2 using deprecated peer encoding","protocol version 2 or later using LogConfiguration","voter/non-voter/staging promotion","add, remove, demote, promote, and address update","configuration request with prevIndex"],"unknowns":["The supplied excerpts do not show all configuration request admission and commit completion paths.","The exact behavior of configuration state during snapshot restore and log suffix replacement needs review.","The protocol-version branch for LogConfiguration application is only partially shown."],"source_ids":["configuration.go:129:310","raft.go:1203:1390","raft.go:1440:1605","config.go:1:80"]},{"class_id":"A5","applicability":"applicable","purpose":"Turn committed log decisions into FSM state-machine effects and client-visible responses.","realization_summary":"processLogs skips already-applied indices, loads committed entries from futures or LogStore, filters non-FSM log types, batches applicable entries, sends them to the FSM mutation channel, and updates last-applied state. FSM.Apply or optional ApplyBatch produces response values returned through futures. Barriers are sent to the FSM; no-ops and some configuration entries are filtered.","entry_points":["Raft.processLogs","Raft.prepareLog","FSM.Apply","BatchingFSM.ApplyBatch"],"variants":["single-entry FSM","BatchingFSM","LogCommand","LogBarrier","LogConfiguration","LogNoop and deprecated configuration entries","shutdown while enqueueing FSM work"],"unknowns":["The FSM worker, response correlation, and exact ordering between FSM completion and last-applied updates are not shown.","The supplied excerpt does not establish whether the last-applied update represents dispatch or completed FSM execution.","The complete restore interaction with application state is not shown."],"source_ids":["raft.go:1203:1390","fsm.go:1:80","log.go:1:80"]},{"class_id":"A6","applicability":"applicable","purpose":"Persist, publish, compact, delete, and reconstruct protocol history and recovery evidence.","realization_summary":"Leaders and followers write logs through LogStore. Snapshot execution obtains FSM state, captures committed configuration metadata, creates and persists a snapshot, closes it, records last-snapshot metadata, and deletes old logs while retaining configured trailing logs. Snapshot creation is blocked when the FSM-applied index is behind the committed configuration index.","entry_points":["Raft.dispatchLogs","raft.appendEntries","Raft.runSnapshots","Raft.takeSnapshot","Raft.compactLogsWithTrailing","Raft.removeOldLogs"],"variants":["automatic snapshot interval","user-triggered snapshot","snapshot persistence failure","snapshot close failure","log compaction with trailing logs","restore-related old-log removal"],"unknowns":["Concrete LogStore, SnapshotStore, and sink durability/atomicity are not supplied.","Snapshot replacement, cleanup of failed snapshots, and startup reconstruction are not fully shown.","The exact ordering and failure recovery after snapshot close but before compaction require review."],"source_ids":["raft.go:1203:1390","raft.go:1440:1605","snapshot.go:72:278","fsm.go:1:80","log.go:1:80"]},{"class_id":"A7","applicability":"applicable","purpose":"Admit client operations, report leadership and commit outcomes, and expose applied or rejected work.","realization_summary":"Follower paths reject leader-only requests with ErrNotLeader. Leader setup dispatches client logs and responds to in-flight futures on leadership loss, restore supersession, shutdown, or persistence errors. Apply and Barrier semantics distinguish committed log processing from FSM application, but the complete public API and future lifecycle are not supplied.","entry_points":["Raft.runFollower request channels","Raft.leaderLoop","Raft.dispatchLogs","logFuture.respond","client Apply and Barrier APIs"],"variants":["leader admission","follower rejection","leadership loss","snapshot restore supersession","enqueue timeout","shutdown","Apply versus Barrier"],"unknowns":["The complete client API and future implementation are not included in the supplied excerpts.","Caller retry, identity, cancellation, and duplicate-operation semantics are not established.","The exact point at which ApplyFuture success is exposed relative to durable commit and FSM completion needs review."],"source_ids":["api.go:1:80","docs/README.md:1:80","raft.go:135:340","raft.go:468:700","raft.go:1203:1390"]}],"behaviors":[{"id":"B1","primary_activity":"A2","execution_owner":"Raft main thread","protocol_context":"follower state","trigger":"Heartbeat timer expires after no recent successful leader contact.","legal_preconditions":["Raft is in follower state.","The latest configuration is available.","The local server is a voter in the relevant stable configuration."],"implementation_guards":["Heartbeat timeout has elapsed.","The latest configuration is non-empty.","The latest configuration is committed and includes the local voter before election is started."],"reads":["current Raft state","last contact time","latest and committed configuration","local server ID"],"writes":["Raft state to Candidate","cleared leader address and ID"],"durable_effects":[],"external_effects":["Election progression is initiated by the candidate loop."],"important_branches":["No known peers: remain follower.","Not in stable voter configuration: do not start election.","Local voter after timeout: enter Candidate."],"async_boundaries":["Returns from follower loop to the main run loop, which enters candidate behavior."],"produces_fact_ids":["F2"],"consumes_fact_ids":["F1"],"cross_activity_effects":[{"key":"A1","value":"May initiate a new authority context that governs later log formation."},{"key":"A7","value":"Clears leader information used by client-facing leader discovery."}],"existing_protections":["Voter membership check","Stable configuration check","Heartbeat timeout"],"source_ids":["raft.go:135:340"],"unknowns":["The supplied excerpt does not show term persistence at the exact state transition."]},{"id":"B2","primary_activity":"A2","execution_owner":"Raft main thread","protocol_context":"candidate state","trigger":"Candidate loop starts after follower timeout or another transition.","legal_preconditions":["Raft is Candidate.","Election term is derived from current term."],"implementation_guards":["Pre-vote is skipped for configured disabled mode or leadership transfer.","Vote tally is compared with quorum size.","Newer-term responses can return the node to follower."],"reads":["current term","pre-vote configuration","leadership-transfer flag","quorum size","vote responses"],"writes":["current term on newer response","Raft state on election outcome","leadership-transfer flag reset"],"durable_effects":["Vote persistence occurs in the receiver behavior B5, not in this tally behavior."],"external_effects":["Vote and pre-vote RPCs are sent through Transport."],"important_branches":["Pre-vote denied or newer term","quorum reached","election timeout","leadership transfer vote path"],"async_boundaries":["Vote and pre-vote results arrive asynchronously through channels."],"produces_fact_ids":["F3"],"consumes_fact_ids":["F2"],"cross_activity_effects":[{"key":"A1","value":"A successful election establishes the authority context under which a leader can dispatch entries."},{"key":"A7","value":"Leader state changes affect admission and in-flight client futures."}],"existing_protections":["Quorum calculation","Term comparison","Leadership-transfer flag reset"],"source_ids":["raft.go:135:340"],"unknowns":["The supplied excerpt stops before the complete vote tally and leader promotion logic."]},{"id":"B3","primary_activity":"A1","execution_owner":"Leader main thread","protocol_context":"leader log dispatch","trigger":"Leader receives a client log, no-op, barrier, or configuration log to dispatch.","legal_preconditions":["Raft is Leader.","The request has passed leader-loop admission."],"implementation_guards":["A log index and current term are assigned.","The entry is stored in LogStore before replication notification.","Leadership-loss and store-error branches respond to futures."],"reads":["current term","last log index","leader replication state","client future or internal log future"],"writes":["log index and term on entry","in-flight future list","last-log metadata","local commitment match"],"durable_effects":["LogStore.StoreLogs persists